lms — third-party attribution
=============================

Provenance
----------

Clean-room implementation from RFC 8554 ("Leighton-Micali Hash-Based
Signatures", IRTF/CFRG, April 2019), a public specification: LM-OTS (§4),
LMS (§5), HSS (§6), the wire formats of §3.3 and the pseudorandom key
generation of Appendix A were implemented from the RFC text alone. No
implementation of LMS/HSS was read, run or ported (not cisco/hash-sigs, not
pyhsslms, not Bouncy Castle, not any other). Uses only the Zig standard
library (`std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256`).

Attribution (a condition, as for every RFC quotation in this repository)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

`src/kat_vectors.zig` reproduces, unaltered, the known-answer data of
RFC 8554 Appendix F (Test Cases 1 and 2: public keys, messages, HSS
signatures, and the Test Case 2 SEED and I values). It is IETF material,
reproduced under the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions (TLP 5.0 §3.c.iii) with
this attribution: "RFC 8554, Appendix F, Copyright (c) 2019 IETF Trust and the
persons identified as the authors of the RFC (D. McGrew, M. Curcio,
S. Fluhrer)". Redistributing this module, alone or as part of zig-libs,
keeps this file with it. No other third-party material is present.
